WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.381
Hey! Welcome to a new Project Kamp update video!

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:05.323
This video is highly requested by you guys!

00:00:05.323 --> 00:00:08.680
We're going to do a review on
 our battery powered electric chainsaw.

00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:11.300
And, our brush cutter...

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.160
You guys have been asking for it,
but we didn't make a review yet...

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.840
Because, we want to give a real review,
after really using the tool for a longer period of time.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.400
So, this is one year later.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.000
Both machines are Makita battery-powered,
and just do point it out: we're not sponsored...

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
We actually tried to remove the brands as much as we can.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.801
Because, we just want to give an unbiased opinion.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:36.160
And, to make sure we're not sponsored,
or need to say anything.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.560
So, this video, we're going to have a look at them.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.840
We're going to do a contest also between
an electric and a gas powered one.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.840
We're going to test them, and see all the pros and cons.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.800
But, in order to start this whole review,
we need to go back one year in time.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.040
So, in today's update, we have something new.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.160
It's an electric chainsaw.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.840
I never really worked
with an electric chainsaw before.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.640
That sounds kind of impressive to me!

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.520
Less noise.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.800
That's the main reason why we have it.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.840
And, it doesn't run on fossil fuels.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.159
So, this video, I want to put it together, test it...

00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:25.720
One of few things I'm particularly interested in is: 
"How long does it actually last?"

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.640
Because, one saw has two batteries,
and I have six batteries in total.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.520
So I can have three sessions, and I'm curious...

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.120
To see how long they last before they're empty.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.600
How much noise does it make?

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.760
And also, how I don't know how robust
and sturdy this machine feels.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.360
It feels a bit like a toy almost.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.920
It's a small, but important note:
this video is not sponsored by Makita!

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.920
We bought the machine 
from people supporting us on Patreon.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.815
You might wonder why we did get a Makita...

00:01:52.815 --> 00:01:57.320
Basically, because our power tools are already
running on their battery system.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.752
So, we kind of locked into that system, 
which in a way feels bad.

00:02:01.752 --> 00:02:05.240
Because, you're stuck in an ecosystem, 
and might not use the best saw...

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.720
But, you just choose it, because it fits the rest.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.478
That, in a way, is also the powerful thing.

00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:12.639
Once you have a battery, you can use it on your different devices.

00:02:12.639 --> 00:02:14.520
I get it that it has ups and downs...

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.560
So, we're going to chop down some bushes,
some trees that I didn't do last time...

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.221
Big, small, wet, old, new, fresh...

00:02:23.221 --> 00:02:24.160
All sorts of trees.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.541
We have the saw.

00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:27.031
Cardboard, cardboard...

00:02:27.443 --> 00:02:28.462
The chain.

00:02:28.462 --> 00:02:29.412
Chain oil.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.400
The thing that holds the chain.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.400
And, the batteries, which we already had ourselves.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.680
We're going to start off simple, by chopping some dead trees.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.160
I'm not sure if you've seen this...

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.080
In Update 3, I made a few pathways right there.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.720
But, I left quite a bunch of bigger trees over there,
because I didn't want to cut them.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.280
Now, I'm going to clean this all up,
and chop them with a chainsaw.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.240
This looks like a good first cut!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.200
That's kind of impressive, actually!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.640
The path is now clear, which went surprisingly fast actually!

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.800
The saw itself looks good!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.678
A bit dusty...

00:04:20.678 --> 00:04:23.720
The battery life is two dots, whatever that means...

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.000
I mean, I'm kind of surprised, actually,
with how smooth this went.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.373
But, to be fair, these are already dead trees.

00:04:31.373 --> 00:04:32.771
They burned down a few years ago.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:35.800
So, in a way, I would say an easy score as well.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.880
For the next part, we're going to the swamp.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.160
Because, a few weeks ago, I cleaned it,
and I took out a lot of trees.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.960
All those trees need to be chopped into smaller trees.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.520
This test is basically to just do a lot of cutting.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.000
So, here are a bunch of trees,
and I'm just going to chop them down.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.760
New batteries!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.000
All right, so, all the wood is now chopped,
which is quite a lot actually.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.240
It went super fast, and super smooth!

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.160
Maybe, it's just because it's new, that it's all fun...

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.997
But, I'm kind of still surprised how smooth it goes!

00:05:43.997 --> 00:05:47.440
Halfway in, the batteries were empty,
so we had to change them.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.275
Just swap in other ones, and it's done.

00:05:49.275 --> 00:05:50.785
Also, that's smooth!

00:05:50.785 --> 00:05:52.654
Now, the battery's half empty again.

00:05:52.654 --> 00:05:56.768
So, I would say doing all of this took me one battery pack.

00:05:56.768 --> 00:05:58.149
So, two batteries in total.

00:05:58.149 --> 00:06:04.108
Now, we go to the next part,
where we're going to chop just a few bigger trees.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.280
And finally, we have this pile!

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.282
You might have seen it in Update 3,
where I make the pathways.

00:06:10.282 --> 00:06:15.277
This was such a big pile of just trees,
that I never cleaned it.

00:06:15.277 --> 00:06:18.166
I always walk over it, which is far from ideal...

00:06:18.166 --> 00:06:20.166
Not proud of it, but...

00:06:20.166 --> 00:06:22.640
Yeah, maybe now is the time to clean it up!

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.080
So, for this test, we have one full battery.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.240
I'm just going to put on a timelapse,
and chop to see how fast it goes.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.720
And, how much battery it takes,
 to get rid of this pile.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.394
So, this job is not finished yet,
and I'm out of batteries...

00:07:01.394 --> 00:07:05.280
Now, I did work a bit intensively,
with a lot of thick wood in a very short time.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.120
But, yeah, the job is just not finished yet,
and the batteries are empty...

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.200
With a normal chainsaw,
you could just add fuel and continue.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.760
And, with this one you have to recharge...

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.240
So, I'll continue tomorrow,
which is perfectly fine for me.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.520
But, if you're in the middle in the job,
I could see that being a bit annoying.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:28.200
But, for now, since we can't cut anyway, 
let's open this one up to see how it's made.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.680
So, a final verdict!

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.080
I would say it's a pretty good saw, and nice to work with!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.848
But, I would also say:
"Don't really believe anything I'm saying."

00:08:07.848 --> 00:08:12.400
Because, I'm not at all experienced with chainsaws,
and it's the first time I'm using it...

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.920
So, obviously, everything is exciting,
and everything is still good and proper.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:21.600
I think the test is really about time, like:
"Is it still durable after a while?"

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.813
Does everything stay properly?

00:08:22.813 --> 00:08:23.972
Doesn't the stuff break?

00:08:23.972 --> 00:08:27.658
So, I would say: 
"Make sure to remind me in a year or something."

00:08:27.658 --> 00:08:30.480
To make a review, or to talk about this thing...

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.440
Because then, I could give a real honest review about it.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.720
But, I would say: so far, so good.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:40.400
All right, so, here we are: it's one year later.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.456
This is what this looks like now.

00:08:42.456 --> 00:08:43.840
It's a bit more worn out.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.960
We used it heavily, but it still functions as it did before.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.280
I actually forgot to mention the model before...

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:54.360
It's a DUC353, in case you're curious...

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:00.716
And, as we were using this throughout the year, 
we actually also bought an electric brush cutter.

00:09:00.936 --> 00:09:04.516
because, it's the same battery system,
and we kind of liked working with the electric tools.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.600
So, we got one of these as well.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:11.480
This one is the DUR369A.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.320
So, I'm going to show you it a little bit as well.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.200
How this one is being used, and whether we like it or not.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.920
Because, we've also been using it for a year.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.920
But, looking back at the footage...

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:30.320
One year ago from saw, I was kind of excited when we got it,
because it felt super powerful.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.240
Quick cuts!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:34.480
But, that was also because I was mainly 
comparing it with a handsaw.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.960
So, yeah, obviously a chainsaw is a bit
more superior than this one.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.200
What I actually needed to do
is to don't compare it with the handsaw...

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.360
But, instead, compare it with a chainsaw, 
because this is kind of the competitor of this one.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:53.041
This is a saw we got from a friend,
and we have been using this electric saw.

00:09:53.041 --> 00:09:54.620
Both throughout the whole year.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.000
We've been using both.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.800
So, now, we have a pretty good reference
between how they compare to each other.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.960
And, I would say, the main thing that is
different is actually just the power.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.760
This thing has way more power than this one.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:11.759
Let me actually show you in a little contest,
if we're going to use this one, compared to this one.

00:10:11.759 --> 00:10:13.440
To see what the difference is.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.480
So, here we have our setup.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.240
Here we have one big log!

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.720
We chopped in the middle, and then we put in like this.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.400
So, this side is exactly the same as this side.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.520
We're going to chop them
 with a gas saw and an electric saw.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.480
And, we're going to see which one is fastest to start.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.200
How long can they cut?

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.400
Which one cuts the fastest?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.480
So, we're just going to start,
and you guys can see how it's going to be.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.600
You can count.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.583
- When we will start?

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.680
Three, two, one!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.920
I had a biscuit that rolled away!

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.240
12 and a half!

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.840
When you have a super sharp thing,
also in the beginning, it cuts super slick.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.520
But, if it's not very sharp,
it cuts not good at all.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.280
And, this one still cuts...

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.968
- They seem pretty similar.

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:51.457
Now, the only way to settle this is a battle!

00:12:51.457 --> 00:12:54.000
And then, we just gear up, and we will cut this!

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.371
Right, so, the winner is this one!

00:12:57.371 --> 00:13:00.040
Tim got 13 slices, and I cut nine in the same time.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:06.120
My battery is almost empty as well,
so I would have to stop soon or Tim could continue.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.120
So, yeah, let's say this one has a bit more power.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.280
Now back to the review!

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:18.600
Okay, so, here we have the pro and con of this machine.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:24.200
The pro is that it's quite quiet, 
compared to the gas-powered machine.

00:13:33.274 --> 00:13:35.616
So, soundwise it's much less.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.960
It's also much easier to start.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.393
You just press a button, and you're good to go!

00:13:40.393 --> 00:13:43.246
With the gas saw, you have to pull the cord a few times.

00:13:43.246 --> 00:13:46.601
It also depends on the motor, if it's hot or cold.

00:13:46.601 --> 00:13:49.360
So, yeah, it takes a bit more effort to do.

00:13:54.615 --> 00:13:58.330
Which makes it, as a third pro, very friendly to use.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.760
Especially, people here that haven't 
worked much with a chainsaw.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.640
This is much easier to just grab,
and you take it and you cut something.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.680
And, finally, it just doesn't use any gas,
and it's just a kind of magical!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.000
It just runs on electricity, and in our case, it's solar.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.120
So, in a way, it's just free energy flowing in

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:20.829
You can use it as much as there's energy available

00:14:20.966 --> 00:14:22.017
The downsides on this saw.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.080
It's empty quick, and runs on two batteries.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:29.680
But, once the batteries are empty,
you have to recharge them.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.040
And, this takes a while...

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.040
Meanwhile, you can't do anything,
unless you have more batteries.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.520
It's not as powerful...

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.680
We've been mainly chopping young, fresh trees here.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.720
Which are kind of easy to cut, compared to a thick old tree.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.760
So, it's good to cut some basic little things.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:51.360
But, if you really want to cut a lot,
it's a bit challenging with this one...

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.880
And, it's also hard to fix.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:56.880
Like, mechanically, parts like the chain are the same.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.362
And, the locking mechanisms.

00:14:58.362 --> 00:15:01.480
But, the whole motor is all electrical driven.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.840
So, if something is broken, you can't fix it.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.840
Like, with a combustion engine,
you really have to bring it to Makita.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Where they can change it or replace it.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:13.615
So, those are the differences a bit,
between the two types of saws.

00:15:13.615 --> 00:15:16.287
But, they actually also have a lot of similarities!

00:15:16.287 --> 00:15:22.238
Both have a brake, both have a handle,
both have a chain and a mechanism to cut...

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.682
And, both also need to use the chainsaw oil.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:31.240
Actually, one little tip on that, 
you also have this thing called biodegradable oil.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:35.640
Which I would recommend, and it seems nicer,
if you cut it in the middle of nature.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.440
I would also have one extra other tip,
in terms of sharpening the chains.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.720
So, you're going to need to sharpen the chains,
after using the chainsaw.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.160
And, usually, you do this with a file,
 so you go over the teeth and you sharpen it.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.560
But, there's kind of an art to it,
and especially in this setting with us.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:57.000
Where multiple people use the chainsaw,
you don't want one person to clean it all the time...

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.000
But, learning how to clean a chainsaw
 can be quite challenging.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.680
You need to have the angle right,
to make sure you sharpen it.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.560
So, we also discovered this tool, which we like a lot actually.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:10.560
Because, it sort of explains how to sharpen it.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.710
This thing defines the angle.

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:17.520
So, it makes sure you put it perpendicular to the chain,
and you always go in the right direction.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.280
You make sure it's horizontal.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:24.800
And, it also chops down this smaller part here,
 in front of the chain.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:28.240
Which you usually wouldn't even sharpen with this one.

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:32.760
But, every now and then you also need to do that,
to really make sure the chain sharp.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.800
So, this tool does all of that.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.560
It's very easy for people that are not 
very experienced with a chainsaw...

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.720
To sharpen the chain after using it.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.960
Just a little tip: if you work with multiple people, 
I would recommend this thing.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.840
Okay, so, that was a rough review for chainsaws.

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.240
Next, we're going to go quickly over to brush cutter as well.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.480
A lot of similarity, but also a few differences.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.880
So, let me show you.

00:16:56.375 --> 00:16:56.875
All right!

00:16:56.875 --> 00:16:59.560
Here, we have the brush cutter.

00:17:02.307 --> 00:17:07.800
It looks pretty similar to a usual brush cutter,
as with the chainsaw, except this one works on battery.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.600
It also slides in two batteries.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.280
The same as the chainsaw.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:15.280
And then, you have three different speeds that you can use.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.520
We've been using this one for over a year as well.

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:23.824
We've done a lot of rough things with it, I would say.

00:17:23.824 --> 00:17:26.163
A few complications with it as well...

00:17:26.163 --> 00:17:27.989
Here, the plastic cover broke.

00:17:27.989 --> 00:17:32.705
I would say it's on us, because probably some stone
 or something chopped in there...

00:17:32.705 --> 00:17:36.480
It doesn't really seem to be the issue of the machine.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.880
However, we did have two electrical issues as well.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:42.880
One was right after we bought it,
and one a few weeks ago.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:44.640
It then just gives an error.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.240
You can't really do anything, besides bringing it to Makita...

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:51.240
And then, it was a nice again,
as it came back a few weeks later.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.480
But yeah, that were a bit of the downsides...

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:57.840
And, for this machine, it works also pretty similar,
as the usual brush cutter.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.000
So, you have a few blades you can use.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.360
Let me actually show those!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:06.480
So, when we first started brush cutting,
you had all these different kind of blades...

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:10.600
We didn't really know what they meant,
or how to use them for what purpose.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.120
So, I'm quickly going to show you.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.120
Because, I think is very useful information,
when you start brush cutting.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.240
So, we have a string cutter like this,
with a little nylon cord.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.240
It's good for chopping grass.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.280
But, the moment you want to chop something thicker, 
this breaks, which is not ideal.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.400
It also leaves plastic around...

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:27.957
So, you need something bigger.

00:18:27.957 --> 00:18:30.920
What we like to use is this triangular blade.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:32.840
This is kind of an all rounder.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.720
It's good in just chopping and it can chop thicker things.

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:41.015
It's also good for mulching, so you can really make, 
whatever you're going to cut, small.

00:18:41.015 --> 00:18:44.040
So, it could chop grass, but also more like brambles.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:45.800
Like, bigger things.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:51.760
If you really want to cut a lot of brambles, 
which we've been doing a lot, like big bushes above you...

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:56.040
You can use a blade like this,
with the blades going downwards.

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:00.720
Because, you can really go from top to bottom,
 and it sort of chops everything underneath there.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.400
It's a bit more aggressive to use,
but very effective for thick brambles.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:10.128
We recently had it inserted with this blade,

00:19:10.128 --> 00:19:11.749
It feels very rough to me!

00:19:11.749 --> 00:19:15.973
It's just a circular saw blade,
and just spinning there in front of you.

00:19:15.973 --> 00:19:21.240
I guess, I'm used to working with tablesaws,
where everything is very fixed and safe with perfection covers.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.240
And, here you are, just swinging with the blade!

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:30.208
But, this made me used to chop more 
smaller trees and branches in front of you.

00:19:30.208 --> 00:19:33.082
So, you can just sort of have a saw in front of you.

00:19:33.082 --> 00:19:34.160
Just chopping the things...

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:38.800
The blade we use mainly is this one,
because a bit of an all-rounder.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:42.440
You can go to things like grass,
but also thicker bushes.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.040
It sort of just chops!

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:47.280
And, we also like to use this one,
if we really take on big brambles.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.640
The blade itself, the saw blade: I don't like it...

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.640
This one every now and then,
 if we really do the grass.

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:58.680
But, yeah, this is just standard information for brush cutters,
but just not specifically for electric ones.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:03.040
So, now, let's get back to why 
this electric one is different than a gas one.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.180
All right!

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.080
Here, we have to review of the brush cutter,
 with the pros and the cons.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:12.610
They're very similar to the chainsaw,
as in, it's also less noisy, because it's electric.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:15.920
It's easier to start, and it doesn't use any gas.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.640
So, you can just run it on electricity, which is cool.

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:22.080
And, the downside is that it's also hard to repair.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:25.983
It can really open it up, and it doesn't last super long.

00:20:25.983 --> 00:20:28.280
The battery life, and the sort of endurance is not very high...

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:31.880
However, the main difference is that it does have enough power.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.640
It really feels it's good, unlike with the chainsaw.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.200
So, those were the two reviews 
of the brush cutters and the chainsaws!

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.400
Now, let me give you a final verdict,
of both of these electric machines.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:48.160
All right, here's the final verdict of these two machines,
 used for one year in our setting.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:51.240
So, a big plus for us is that they just make less noise.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.920
Because, we're here with many people in this land,
 so we easily disturb each other...

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.120
The less noise they make, the better!

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.846
Second one: it's quite friendly to use!

00:20:59.846 --> 00:21:04.680
Because, you don't need to deal with the gas, 
the starting, the hot or cold engine...

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:09.360
Also, the moment you don't use it,
you don't have to have it run idle.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:12.360
You can just turn it off and turn it back
 on again, when you need it.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:15.960
Which makes this whole process much more friendly,
 than with the gas-powered device.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:19.200
I mean, it's running on solar,
which is the main reason why we have it.

00:21:20.025 --> 00:21:24.480
We're here off-grid, so we can just use the electricity
and we put it directly in the machines.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:28.080
It's kind of magical, and they're
pretty good to just quickly do something!

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.458
Because, you just pick up the machine, and you can start.

00:21:30.458 --> 00:21:34.680
You don't have this hole start-up, 
like the gas-powered machine.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:38.640
Now, two main downsides: 
I would say the chainsaw is a little bit of a joke...

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:41.720
It's if you really want a chainsaw for bigger trunks,
 or a lot of them.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:47.164
It's nice here and there, but if you really want a chainsaw,
for multiple hours in a row...

00:21:47.494 --> 00:21:49.370
I wouldn't recommend this thing.

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:51.280
The brush cutter has less of this problem.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:53.520
It feels like it's really made for a job.

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:58.920
But, the downside that both of them have 
is that they consume quite a lot of batteries...

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:03.640
For us, it's less of a problem, because we have already this 
whole Makita system with a lot of batteries.

00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:06.200
But, if you don't have that,
you need to buy a lot of batteries.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:10.120
To make sure, that once they're empty,
 that you can keep going and keep swapping them.

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.680
And, besides that, the charging just also takes time.

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:16.600
With the gas one, you can just keep on going all the time.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.680
You might need to wait for your batteries to be charged...

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:24.343
Besides that, I would say: nice machines to have!

00:22:24.343 --> 00:22:30.840
I, personally, really like to brush cutters, because it's just smooth, 
 compared to a gas powered one to work with.

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:34.080
Quickly start-ups, quickly stops! I like it!

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:39.160
The chainsaw is nice to have around, but I notice myself,
every now and then, I still use the handsaw.

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:41.160
If I want to just cut something smaller.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:44.080
And, if it's thick, it's still too small for that...

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:46.600
But, that's just my personal opinion!

00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:50.960
But, yeah, that was a review of our electric saws!

00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:54.120
That's it! Potato time!

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:01.320
All right, so, that was it for the review video!

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:02.990
Now, I am sharpening the chainsaw.

00:23:02.990 --> 00:23:05.040
Something you always have to do after using it.

